1
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:15,098
You're done now.

2
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:17,142
Those who control auto-tracking Stands…

3
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:19,102
It's F.F.!

4
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:21,104
Why are they at this Disciplinary Wing?

5
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:28,236
He has a disc!

6
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:31,322
Pale Snake is nearby!

7
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:32,907
Where is he?

8
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,120
No way…

9
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:38,413
The one who threw it was…

10
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:40,623
It can't be him!

11
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:43,585
So the one who controls Pale Snake is…

12
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:46,588
You are…

13
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:48,506
Father Pucchi.

14
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:23,017
F.F. feared one thing above all else.

15
00:02:23,101 --> 00:02:26,771
It wasn't the destruction of their body,

16
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:30,233
but the elimination
of their own intellect.

17
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:38,158
I remember everything
since the day I met Jolyne.

18
00:02:39,117 --> 00:02:41,494
The weird graffiti on prison phones,

19
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:44,956
the lint-covered blankets on the bed,
and the smell of garbage.

20
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,041
The guard's shouts,

21
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:51,254
the sounds of doors opening and closing,
and the toilet flushing, even.

22
00:02:52,964 --> 00:02:55,967
Fooling around with Jolyne
and the others and laughing together.

23
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:57,176
I remember them all.

24
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:04,392
But before I met Jolyne at the farm,
though I lived there for years,

25
00:03:04,475 --> 00:03:08,146
all I can recall from that time are
memories that are like a machine's.

26
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:09,939
That's all.

27
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,109
I followed orders
without ever questioning why

28
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:16,154
and spent the days
guarding Pale Snake's discs.

29
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,115
But now, I know

30
00:03:19,198 --> 00:03:22,869
that to live means to make memories.

31
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:26,122
I fear losing them the most.

32
00:03:28,124 --> 00:03:30,501
Jolyne is on a mission to save her father

33
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:34,589
and is willing to risk her life
for the ones she cares about like Ermes.

34
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:37,967
That's probably because
she has good memories of them.

35
00:03:38,843 --> 00:03:41,930
That's what powers humans up.

36
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:45,808
Memories give humans
power to keep going at a cellular level.

37
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:50,772
This is an understanding that I,
F.F., lacked before meeting Jolyne.

38
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:53,358
That's right.

39
00:03:54,275 --> 00:03:55,193
That is…

40
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:59,239
That is what it means
to be an intelligent being.

41
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:05,328
Which do you prioritize?

42
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:06,955
Is it me?

43
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:10,458
Or is it finishing D an' G?

44
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:17,090
You hesitated for a split second!

45
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:19,676
That will cost you your life!

46
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:31,980
I gave you intellect and a Stand.

47
00:04:33,523 --> 00:04:35,191
I am taking it back.

48
00:04:36,484 --> 00:04:40,738
When I think about Jolyne,
I feel courage swelling up inside me.

49
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:43,700
This is what memories do.

50
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:47,704
This is… my intellect!

51
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:51,666
What?

52
00:04:58,548 --> 00:04:59,632
No…

53
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:03,011
Is F.F. planning to--

54
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:08,433
Their bodily fluids entered his body!

55
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,357
Impossible…

56
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:24,032
Am I…

57
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:32,457
Looks like F.F. did it.

58
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,043
They must have killed its User.

59
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,339
Where is the fruit?

60
00:05:56,272 --> 00:05:57,607
What the hell?

61
00:05:58,691 --> 00:06:00,568
Does this mean that it's born?

62
00:06:01,277 --> 00:06:04,822
Is this what Pale Snake wanted?

63
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:10,912
What the hell is this thing?

64
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:13,706
Why was it given life?

65
00:06:14,248 --> 00:06:16,250
Why does it exist here?

66
00:06:17,001 --> 00:06:20,963
Were the prisoners mutated
just to give life to this thing?

67
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:26,135
Now that it's born,
my body is no longer mutating.

68
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:27,678
It stopped turning into a plant.

69
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:39,440
You must not let F.F. escape!

70
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:41,734
Read the memory inside the disc!

71
00:06:42,318 --> 00:06:47,323
Tell me the whereabouts
of the spawn of Dio's bone!

72
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:50,785
Will I even last 30 seconds
when I'm exposed like this?

73
00:06:50,868 --> 00:06:51,869
I need water.

74
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:56,624
I need to tell Jolyne
who Pale Snake really is!

75
00:06:59,043 --> 00:06:59,877
Shit.

76
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:03,506
I have to tell her that
he's the prison's chaplain, Father Pucchi!

77
00:07:06,634 --> 00:07:10,221
Are you trying to reach the
faucet at the entrance?

78
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:14,433
Before you go,
I have one question for you!

79
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:20,106
You can't escape my Stand!

80
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:43,379
There's one thing I want to ask, F.F.

81
00:07:44,088 --> 00:07:46,048
It's a very simple question.

82
00:07:46,132 --> 00:07:47,592
Did you see it?

83
00:07:48,259 --> 00:07:50,761
Did you see the thing born
at the Disciplinary Wing?

84
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,055
How did it look?

85
00:07:53,556 --> 00:07:55,183
Was it a plant?

86
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:56,726
Was it beautiful?

87
00:07:56,809 --> 00:08:01,647
What is a priest doing
at a prison like this?

88
00:08:01,731 --> 00:08:05,234
I hope you understand that
I'm asking the questions here.

89
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:10,823
I can easily extract your memory
and read it to understand what was born.

90
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:14,869
But I wanted to know how you felt.

91
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:19,999
Things like it looked soft
or that it was beautiful

92
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:24,086
are your opinions, and can't be read
from a memory disc.

93
00:08:24,837 --> 00:08:28,216
Are you worried that the spawn
will escape?

94
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:29,550
You're afraid of losing it.

95
00:08:30,384 --> 00:08:32,512
Is it able to move already?

96
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:33,971
How the hell should I know?

97
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:38,017
I'd be more worried about it
getting destroyed.

98
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:41,729
No, maybe it's already done.

99
00:08:41,812 --> 00:08:44,732
Jolyne is with that mean asshole,
after all.

100
00:08:45,274 --> 00:08:47,818
If she's compelled to,
she'll finish it off.

101
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:50,404
It's impossible to defeat it.

102
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:52,156
That will never happen.

103
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:57,787
No one can destroy it,
that much I know well.

104
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:02,500
My only concern is Jolyne
causing trouble and losing it.

105
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:06,546
Jotaro's memory alone is enough
to control the birthed creature,

106
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:10,132
and I have his memory.

107
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:13,052
We are so close to the end.

108
00:09:13,135 --> 00:09:14,929
What is it shaped like?

109
00:09:15,012 --> 00:09:18,224
Did it grow faster than you expected?

110
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:22,186
I thought it was gonna drown in water.

111
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:25,606
And then, what else was there?

112
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:27,900
Let's see…

113
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,861
It's stalling for time! Turn around!

114
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,283
I did it!

115
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:39,620
My soul isn't in my head,

116
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,497
it's over there.

117
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,541
I have water now!

118
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:46,294
I can go tell Jolyne everything!

119
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:57,305
Your soul, you say?

120
00:09:57,388 --> 00:10:02,393
No matter where your intelligence lies,
you're not the one making decisions here.

121
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:06,689
I am the one who endowed you
with a Stand ability.

122
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:10,443
You filthy plankton!

123
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:14,238
Don't you dare give me explanations,
as if you know better than I do!

124
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:25,833
My body! This water…

125
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:30,046
What is streaming out of it?

126
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:31,672
No, it can't be!

127
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:33,674
It's steaming hot water.

128
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:40,306
No aquatic organism on earth can dwell
in water hotter than 32 degrees Celsius.

129
00:10:40,389 --> 00:10:43,684
A different Stand ability that
turns water into hot water…

130
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,853
…was inserted into this thing.

131
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:49,940
Only I get to decide
where your intellect lies.

132
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:52,526
You are using your own ability to turn

133
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:54,779
the water you touch
into boiling hot water!

134
00:11:08,125 --> 00:11:10,086
Jolyne!

135
00:11:34,068 --> 00:11:35,945
STAND NAME: GREEN, GREEN, GREEN HOME
STAND MASTER: THE GREEN BABY

136
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,198
Where is it? Where did it fall?

137
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:41,951
Shit, don't tell me it drowned.

138
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:46,539
No…

139
00:11:49,208 --> 00:11:51,377
Does it have a mind of its own?

140
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,671
Since it's trying to escape?

141
00:11:54,296 --> 00:11:55,256
No…

142
00:11:55,339 --> 00:11:58,008
Instinct is its only drive.

143
00:11:58,092 --> 00:12:02,221
I don't know whether it's a plant or not,
but I don't want it to go anywhere.

144
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:05,599
I can't let Pale Snake have it.

145
00:12:07,893 --> 00:12:08,811
Jolyne!

146
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:13,899
Wait, Jolyne!

147
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:16,986
Don't move, look at the rock by your foot!

148
00:12:20,489 --> 00:12:21,490
Listen closely.

149
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:22,908
Don't take another step.

150
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:25,202
Turn around and look at me.

151
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:32,960
When the pebble rolled over here,
it turned into a rock.

152
00:12:33,043 --> 00:12:36,172
Meanwhile, Jolyne, you grew smaller.

153
00:12:37,506 --> 00:12:40,384
Stop! I said don't go near it!

154
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:48,434
What just happened, Anastasia?

155
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:51,145
Why did you grow shorter?

156
00:12:57,109 --> 00:13:00,070
- What's going on, Anastasia?
- Stay calm, Jolyne.

157
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:05,367
By the way, how big
does that baby look to you?

158
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:09,538
It hasn't changed.
Its size is the same as before.

159
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:10,915
Anastasia,

160
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:13,959
it looks like you are the one
who grew shorter to me.

161
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:15,127
What's going on?

162
00:13:15,753 --> 00:13:19,215
The baby's size looks
about average to me too.

163
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:21,967
Only the pebble
we kicked over got smaller.

164
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:25,054
Jolyne, don't move.

165
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:27,014
Stay right where you are.

166
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:34,396
You're back to normal.

167
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:37,691
Do you think that
this is the baby's ability?

168
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:42,988
The closer we get to the baby,
the shorter we grow.

169
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,698
I don't have a clue.

170
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:46,951
That's a heavy line of questioning.

171
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:51,872
Now listen, if we get halfway to the baby,

172
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:54,083
my height shrinks by half.

173
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,544
That means we have to walk twice as much.

174
00:13:56,627 --> 00:13:57,670
Okay.

175
00:13:57,753 --> 00:14:00,923
Furthermore, if we get
a fourth of the way to the baby,

176
00:14:01,006 --> 00:14:02,758
then the distance grows by four times.

177
00:14:03,384 --> 00:14:05,594
At one-eighth,
we walk eight times as much.

178
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,847
1/32nd,

179
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:10,391
1/64th,

180
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:12,601
1/128th…

181
00:14:13,143 --> 00:14:14,603
Our body will keep shrinking,

182
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:16,981
while the distance
multiplies more and more.

183
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:18,566
Here is the question.

184
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:22,570
Will we ever reach that baby?

185
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:26,657
I say no, not in an eternity.

186
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:34,707
But in order to get
my father's memory back,

187
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,918
I have to get the baby.

188
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:40,504
- Jolyne.
- Anastasia, we'll think

189
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:43,090
after we've done everything we can!

190
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:47,052
It's her focus.

191
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:50,514
The way Jolyne can fixate
towards one goal.

192
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:55,311
I'm here because I'm drawn to
the way she focuses on one thing.

193
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:57,980
The ability to concentrate
enhances a person's beauty.

194
00:14:58,063 --> 00:15:00,858
Those eyes…

195
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:05,863
In time, I'll have you gaze at me
with that intense focus of yours.

196
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:24,965
Stone Ocean!

197
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:28,636
I'm about to reach it! I can catch it!

198
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:33,474
It's no use, Jolyne.
Pull your thread back!

199
00:15:33,557 --> 00:15:35,976
There is no way to reach the baby!

200
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,436
I can't give up!

201
00:15:37,519 --> 00:15:38,938
There has to be an end.

202
00:15:39,021 --> 00:15:40,898
I mean, it's right there!

203
00:15:44,735 --> 00:15:47,947
What do you say to jumping off from here?

204
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:51,450
If I do, I'll reach an end point.

205
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:53,160
The ground is the finishing point.

206
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:54,912
I have to land at some point!

207
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:57,456
Stop, Jolyne! Don't--

208
00:15:57,539 --> 00:16:00,167
Yes! The ground is right there!

209
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:01,961
I can almost reach it!

210
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:03,295
What's happening?

211
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:05,631
My string…

212
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:13,347
What the hell is that?

213
00:16:18,435 --> 00:16:20,229
Don't tell me…

214
00:16:20,312 --> 00:16:22,356
Is this the baby's Stand?

215
00:16:22,439 --> 00:16:24,775
Damn, haven't I reached the ground yet?

216
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:32,241
It hasn't only grown in size,
but in power as well!

217
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:33,742
Its power has multiplied!

218
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:37,037
This Stand… It appeared
just to drag me down,

219
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:42,376
so I won't ever escape
this never-ending fall!

220
00:16:42,459 --> 00:16:44,003
Stone Ocean!

221
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,800
If this is the baby's ability,

222
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:53,345
then catching the Stand
is the same as catching the User!

223
00:17:04,481 --> 00:17:06,859
I'm shrinking!

224
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:08,861
It's trying to reduce me to nothing!

225
00:17:09,486 --> 00:17:11,363
The end I thought I'd reach
wasn't the ground.

226
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:12,614
It was this Stand!

227
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:20,622
Diver Drive.

228
00:17:34,219 --> 00:17:38,390
The closer you get to the baby,
the smaller you get.

229
00:17:38,474 --> 00:17:40,476
Eventually, you will be
reduced to nothing.

230
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:46,148
I don't know why a baby
with such a powerful Stand was born,

231
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:48,901
but I know he will be an enemy someday.

232
00:17:48,984 --> 00:17:53,030
Jolyne, this baby is your enemy.

233
00:17:53,113 --> 00:17:54,364
But…

234
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:56,116
if there's no way to defeat it,

235
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:59,536
then I really can't let
Pale Snake have it.

236
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:14,843
Anastasia, hold on tight!

237
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:21,266
It threw the rock!

238
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:22,726
Does that mean…

239
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,394
that it's thinking for itself?

240
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:28,232
The baby is now
deliberately using its ability!

241
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:31,068
It's coming. Climb!

242
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:33,904
We need to escape as fast as possible!

243
00:18:33,987 --> 00:18:34,905
Run!

244
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:56,593
No matter how much we chase it,
we will never reach that baby.

245
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:59,596
But at least, we caught the Stand.

246
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:02,224
Jolyne, do you still not see

247
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:05,644
what we were climbing toward?

248
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:08,564
It was a gamble.

249
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:12,317
The baby is intelligent and curious.

250
00:19:12,901 --> 00:19:15,487
Earlier, it touched the bottle I threw.

251
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:18,824
When the baby chooses to touch an object,
its size stays the same.

252
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:22,119
In other words,
the bottle's size hasn't changed.

253
00:19:24,371 --> 00:19:28,041
If we can't catch the baby,
we'll have the baby chase after us.

254
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:29,960
We finally reached the bottle.

255
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:32,713
The Stand is inside the bottle now.

256
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:36,049
All we have to do now
is trap it inside the bottle!

257
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:43,557
But… how are we getting out of here?

258
00:19:46,143 --> 00:19:51,106
I'm having Diver Drive enter
the bottle's wall.

259
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:54,193
It's bringing the mouth to us.
Let's go, Jolyne.

260
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:56,403
Run for it!

261
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:05,913
We finally caught it.

262
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:09,249
We got its User, the baby too.

263
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,341
It's changing its position.

264
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:19,426
It's using the bottle to charge forward!

265
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:27,893
Anastasia!

266
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:29,853
Stone Ocean!

267
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:32,022
Jolyne!

268
00:20:32,105 --> 00:20:33,523
You can't break the bottle.

269
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:36,026
We'll be worse off
if we have to face the Stand!

270
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:40,739
Did the baby have this in mind
when it rolled the bottle?

271
00:20:40,822 --> 00:20:42,699
Shit, we're in deep trouble now!

272
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:45,702
- Don't break the bottle!
- But…

273
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:48,038
At this rate, you're done for!

274
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:17,526
Anastasia, look…

275
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:20,988
What the hell?

276
00:21:21,071 --> 00:21:23,073
What's going on?

277
00:21:23,156 --> 00:21:25,367
Jolyne, looks like…

278
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:30,038
it's interested in the star-shaped
birthmark on your left shoulder.

279
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:35,252
Since it touched you,
we turned back to our original size.

280
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:41,049
The baby has the same birthmark
on its shoulder.

281
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:43,260
What's going on?

282
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:47,139
The baby acts like it has known
Jolyne for a long time.

283
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:52,477
Hey, it looks as if it likes me.

284
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:54,021
What should I do?

285
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:56,857
It likes her? No, that's not it.

286
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:59,151
I have no doubt about it.

287
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:01,194
He will turn against us.

288
00:22:01,278 --> 00:22:05,407
I can only sense endless darkness
from this baby's ability.

289
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:09,911
Yes, we may need this baby

290
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:12,205
to retrieve your father's disc
from Pale Snake,

291
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:15,042
but I must kill it while I can.

292
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
